# Components

Skills: `react-components`, `react-feature-ui`, `coding-standards`, `ui-motion`.

## Do

- Export components as `export const Name: FC<NameProps>` (named export).
- Use the folder triple for UI, Feature, and pages: `Name/Name.tsx` + optional `Name.module.scss` + `index.ts`.
- Keep each component `*.tsx` at most 70 lines; split into `Name/components/<Child>/` with its own folder trio (never flat siblings like `Name/Child.tsx`).
- Extract component logic longer than 10 lines (state clusters, handlers, derived state) into custom hooks under `hooks/` or `Name/hooks/` (`useThing.ts`); keep the component as thin orchestration + JSX.
- Move `useEffect` callbacks longer than 10 lines into `Name/utils/` or `@utils/*` (or a custom hook if React state/lifecycle is needed); keep effects as thin orchestration.
- Give every `<img>` a non-empty meaningful `alt`.
- Use semantic tags; make interactivity a `button`, `a`, or native control instead of `div`/`span` + `onClick`.
- Give icon-only buttons an accessible name.
- Keep card containers non-clickable; stretch an inner `a`/`button` for the hit area.
- Prefer existing Modal/motion patterns, then CSS, then the repo animation package (`ui-motion`).
- Add `memo` / `useMemo` / `useCallback` only when neighbors already do or when profiling requires it.

## Body order

1. hooks
2. derived values
3. handlers
4. early returns
5. JSX

For props typing, CSS Modules, clsx, and scale tokens follow skill `coding-standards`.
